WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.280
I want to take a minute here to insert some
factual basis into the this information that

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:11.410
is being spread very quickly about Donald
Trump's supposedly brilliant economy.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.410
And today I'm not sure

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:16.420
[inaudible] argue with you about economic
lag times and when you attribute an economy

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.420
to one president versus the previous versus
the next, not going to argue about whether

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.300
the stock market is a good indicator of how
the economy is doing overall.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.300
It's not.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.300
We've talked about that before.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.970
That's just not today's topic today.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:38.270
The topic is simply to compare Obama and Trump
on three metrics, the stock market, jobs and

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:39.270
income.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.000
First, let's do income.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.140
Since we have new data there, since Donald
Trump took office, income growth has slowed

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:55.961
down compared to the Obama administration
incomes grew 5.8% from 2014 to 2016 under

00:00:55.961 --> 00:00:57.010
Barack Obama.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:03.810
And then when Donald Trump took over from,
uh, a 2016 to 2018 incomes grew at about half

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.810
of that rate.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:07.600
Now, why don't we have 2019 data yet?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.600
Well, it's not a trick.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.720
People's taxes just haven't been done yet.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.170
Peep taxes aren't due until April 15th or
even October if you take the extension.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.780
So we just don't have the 2019 data yet.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:20.220
Next, let's look at the stock market.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.950
Looking at the S and P 500 the broadest of
the three major indices, you will see that

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:32.860
the S and P 500 gained more than 60% during
Barack Obama's first 37 months.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.159
That's how long Trump's been president.

00:01:34.159 --> 00:01:39.590
So we're comparing first 37 months of each
presidency, you would have gained 60% in the

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:46.020
S and P 500 during Barack Obama's first three
years plus one month while the S and P 500

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:52.840
has gained only 37% during Donald Trump's
first three years plus one month.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.350
And then lastly on jobs, if you, we did this
in its own segment not long ago.

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:04.360
Um, the last three years of Obama's presidency
saw more than 8 million jobs created, whereas

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:13.370
the first three years of Trump's saw almost
20% smaller job growth, only 6.6 million jobs

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:17.590
created that is per the Bureau of labor statistics.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:22.480
So when you put it all together, Obama was
better on income growth.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.780
Income growth has slowed since Trump became
president.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.180
Obama was better on the stock market.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:33.750
When we compare Trump's, uh, full presidency
so far to the equivalent time period under

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:39.090
Barack Obama and Barack Obama was better on
job creation.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:45.760
Was it that the recovery that Barack Obama
was overseeing was solely responsible for

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.760
this?

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.240
Well, that wouldn't really explain the job
growth at the end of Barack Obama's presidency.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:55.570
So what you have to understand here is I am
not giving you this information to tell you

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:58.300
that there's nothing good happening in Trump's
economy.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.250
There are people who have done well in Trump's
economy.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.250
There's no question.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:05.940
There are indicators that look okay in Trump's
economy, and I am not telling you this to

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:11.820
pretend that everything about Barack Obama's
economy was ginger snaps and waterfalls.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.160
When we look at different indicators, we get
different results and for a lot of people,

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:20.020
the economy hasn't been good under Trump and
it wasn't good under Barack Obama.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:27.739
The point is when they pick the metrics to
hang their hats on and we look at those metrics

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:35.450
and see that Trump is underperforming Obama,
you have to see the brazen and deceptive nature

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:37.370
of what they are trying to sell you.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:43.050
The disinformation propaganda, I'm glad to
debate how do we really tell how an economy

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.700
is doing and it requires more than three metrics.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.700
That's for sure.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:52.020
And we've talked about that before, but what
we can't allow is not just for them to set

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:53.020
the narrative.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:57.510
It's bad enough when they set the narrative,
but to set the narrative based on misleading

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.040
facts or things that are not actually factual.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.460
That's the point of showing you this information.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.460
Today.

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:09.760
I tweeted an image summarizing all of this,
uh, yesterday to my Twitter page D Pacman.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:13.340
It's been retweeted a lot and we're doing
everything we can to spread that.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:16.109
These are the numbers and the numbers don't
tell us anything.

00:04:16.109 --> 00:04:21.189
It's sort of like if you accept that climate
change is happening, that doesn't tell us

00:04:21.189 --> 00:04:24.349
what we have to do and what the policies should
be.

00:04:24.349 --> 00:04:29.569
But if we have people who are still spreading
denialist conspiracy theories about climate

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:33.069
change, we're not even going to be able to
have the conversation about what should be

00:04:33.069 --> 00:04:34.339
done.

00:04:34.339 --> 00:04:38.449
Recognizing that stock growth has been slower
under Trump, recognizing that job growth has

00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:40.349
been been lower under Trump.

00:04:40.349 --> 00:04:45.219
It doesn't tell us what has to happen, but
we're starting with the facts and that's where

00:04:45.219 --> 00:04:46.569
we should always be starting

